A||||1||Homicidal||Correct Headlight adjustments?||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||08-07-2000||03:55 AM||||I know this a weird inquiry, but where should my headlights point?<P>I just got my new Super Whites in the mail, and I don't know if they should be pointed more up or down.  <P>And should there be a visible gap between the two headlights, or should they overlap?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-07-2000||03:41 PM||||Nothing weird about it. This is a real problem on the majority of cars with sealed beam type headlights. It's not really hard to get them right. Just takes a bit of time. (In fact I think I'll use this as the basis for another cave topic.)<P>Headlights are aimed by making them "square" to the ground. Look  at the front of the lamp. You'll see 3 little tabs sticking out. the plane created by those tabs should be 90 degrees to the ground.<P>The poor mans headlight aimer:<P>You need a piece of plywood big enough to hit all 3 tabs and a level. (The best "level" is one of those combination squares with the dial level like carpenters use)<P>park the car on as level a surface as you can find. lay the level on the ground in line with the car. look carfully at the bubble and don't forget where it lines up.<P>put the plywood against the 3 tabs on the lamp. (If the glass has a big curve you may have to glue 3 identical blocks to the plywood.) put the level against the plywood.<P>adjust the lamp untill the bubble matches where it was on the ground. The lamp should now be very close to it's designed alignment. <P>At least vertically. <P>You'll still need to work horizontal aim out. This is really easy on Fiero because it's lights don't have anything between them. get another piece of plywood set up for the other light and a very straight, very stiff, piece of somthing that will reach across both lights. Adjust the hoizontal screw untill both lights are flat against the straight edge.<P>As for the other question. beam positions and shapes vary by lamp type. It's may be normal for that lamp. can't say w/o seeing the paterns.<P>If you do both the aimings above and still have some gap then that's the norm for that lamp.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-07-2000).]||||reg||1
